rofile_sensitivity_class\": {\"value\": \"U0D0\"},\n  \"flow_conditioner_required\": {\"value\": \"No\"},\n  \"length\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 105, \"max\": null}, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n  \"reverse_flow\": {\"value\": \"Designed to measure\"},\n  \"mechanical_environment_class\": {\"value\": \"B, O\"},\n  \"electromagnetic_environment_class\": {\"value\": \"E2\"},\n  \"temperature_range_ambient\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 70}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  \"power_supply_type\": {\"value\": \"Non replaceable battery\", \"footnote_markers\": [\"1\"]},\n  \"power_supply_voltage_max\": {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\", \"footnote_markers\": [\"1\"]},\n  \"power_supply_voltage_min\": {\"value\": 1.9, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\", \"footnote_markers\": [\"1\"]},\n  \"minimum_battery_lifetime\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"years\"},\n  \"software_version\": {\"value\": \"0.6.28, 1.0.1\", \"footnote_markers\": [\"1\"]},\n  \"crc_checksum_of_legally_relevant_software\": {\"value\": \"0x854EBACF, 0x13372073, 0x3A681C19, 0x1d901C40\"},\n  \"software_type\": {\"value\": \"P (built-for-purpose, embedded)\"},\n  \"software_extensions\": {\"value\": \"I1 (Water meters), S (Software separation), D (Download of Legally Relevant Software)\"}\n}\n\nFootnote markers format: markdown shows \"¹\" and defined as \"1)\". I'll use \"1\".\n\nEvery value object must include unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers per strict shape. For string values, unit null. I'll include all four keys for type_level. That's ~35 entries × ~30 tokens = ~1000 tokens. Fine.\n\nFor model_level values entries, schema example shows plain {model, value}. I'll keep those minimal.\n\nShould I include \"unit\" or \"unit_symbol\" key in model_level? Schema yaml says `attribute, unit, values[]` but example uses \"unit_symbol\". I'll use \"unit_symbol\" as in the example.\n\nrecommendation: {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [2]}.\n\ncertificate.project_number: omitted (not present). oiml_issuer_id omitted.\n\nissuing_authority: maybe also website? Not given. phone/email not given. person_title for Jan Kalandra not given. But the signatory Pavel Klenovský \"Head of Certification Body\" — the schema fields person_responsible/person_title; I could interpret the signatory as the responsible person. Page 1 explicitly \"Person responsible: Jan Kalandra\". I'll set person_responsible \"Jan Kalandra\" and omit title. Could add a second? Schema is single-valued. Keep Jan Kalandra. Hmm — but then Klenovský info lost. Not critical.\n\nCategory: schema example list includes \"Measuring system\", \"Gas meter\", \"Water meter\" not listed but category is free: \"Water meter\".\n\ncertified_type.description: include full description text (English). Reasonably long. I'll include the key sentences.\n\nNow counts: models list 56 entries like {\"model_id\": \"Smartio DN15 Q3=1.6 R=40\"}. ~15 tokens each → 840 tokens. model_level: 6 attributes × 56 values, each value ~ {\"model\": \"Smartio DN15 Q3=1.6 R=40\", \"value\": 0.04} ~ 18 tokens → ~6000 tokens. matrix rows: 56 rows × ~30 tokens → 1700. Total output maybe ~12k tokens. Acceptable.\n\nAlternatively shorten model_id: \"DN15-1.6-40\" meaning? Clarity beats brevity; keep readable: \"DN15 Q3=1.6 R=40\". Drop \"Smartio\" prefix since family_name is Smartio. Use \"DN15 Q3=1.6 R=40\". Good.\n\nLet me now also double check \"≤ 630 1 for Q3=1.6m3/h\" for DN15 — includes R630 for Q3=1.6 ✓ (table3 col1). And \"≤1000 for Q3=4\" DN20 ✓.\n\nAlso marking lists \"Δp 10, Δp 16, Δp 25\" and photo shows DN25 Q3=2.5 R=1600 — that's just a sample photo; certificate tables only DN15/DN20. Keep as is.\n\nWrite footnotes text exactly: \"The ratio Q3 / Q1 shall be chosen according to paragraph 4.1.4 of OIML R 49-1:2013\". Subscripts flattened: \"Q3/Q1\".\n\nNow assemble JSON carefully. Ensure valid JSON (no trailing commas, escaped quotes in connection types: use \\\" escapes: \"NPSM or G type ¾\\\", 7/8\\\", 1\\\"\" — better convert ¾ to \"3/4\". I'll write \"NPSM or G type 3/4\\\", 7/8\\\", 1\\\"\".\n\nAlso m³ superscript: use \"m³\" fine in JSON (UTF-8).\n\nmodel_level entries order: nominal_diameter, q1, q2, q3, q4, ratio_q3_q1.\n\nLet me carefully produce the 56-value arrays in model order:\n\nModel order list (56):\n1 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=40\n2 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=40\n3 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=50\n4 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=50\n5 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=63\n6 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=63\n7 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=80\n8 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=80\n9 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=100\n10 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=100\n11 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=125\n12 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=125\n13 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=160\n14 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=160\n15 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=200\n16 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=200\n17 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=250\n18 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=250\n19 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=315\n20 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=315\n21 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=400\n22 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=400\n23 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=500\n24 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=500\n25 DN15 Q3=1.6 R=630\n26 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=630\n27 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=800\n28 DN15 Q3=2.5 R=1000\n29 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=40\n30 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=40\n31 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=50\n32 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=50\n33 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=63\n34 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=63\n35 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=80\n36 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=80\n37 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=100\n38 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=100\n39 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=125\n40 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=125\n41 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=160\n42 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=160\n43 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=200\n44 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=200\n45 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=250\n46 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=250\n47 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=315\n48 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=315\n49 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=400\n50 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=400\n51 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=500\n52 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=500\n53 DN20 Q3=2.5 R=630\n54 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=630\n55 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=800\n56 DN20 Q3=4.0 R=1000\n\nnominal_diameter values: 1-28: 15; 29-56: 20.\nq1: \n1: 0.04, 2: 0.063, 3: 0.032, 4: 0.05, 5: 0.025, 6: 0.04, 7: 0.02, 8: 0.031, 9: 0.016, 10: 0.025, 11: 0.013, 12: 0.02, 13: 0.01, 14: 0.016, 15: 0.008, 16: 0.013, 17: 0.006, 18: 0.01, 19: 0.005, 20: 0.008, 21: 0.004, 22: 0.006, 23: 0.003, 24: 0.005, 25: 0.0025, 26: 0.004, 27: 0.003, 28: 0.0025, 29: 0.063, 30: 0.1, 31: 0.05, 32: 0.08, 33: 0.04, 34: 0.064, 35: 0.031, 36: 0.05, 37: 0.025, 38: 0.04, 39: 0.02, 40: